@startuml feature_v4_F-004_sequence
' Runtime truth for F-004 v4 — Secret and token lifecycle
' The cast below is the `participants:` list of feature_v4_F-004_front-matter.yaml, name for name.
' One group per story; one group per failure mode the front matter declares.
title F-004 v4 — Secret and token lifecycle
autonumber

actor "Security reviewer" as Reviewer
participant "Terraform root" as Terraform
participant "saas-token-rotator" as Rotator
participant "akvwriter" as Writer
participant "AKV expiry validator" as ExpiryGate
participant "Metrics endpoint" as Metrics
participant "SaaS token API" as Saas
database "Secret catalogue" as Catalogue
database "Key Vault West Europe" as VaultWE
database "Key Vault North Europe" as VaultNE
database "mgmt-leader-status ConfigMap" as Status

group F-004-US1 — every platform secret is visible, with who writes it
  Reviewer -> Catalogue : read the two catalogue maps, split by write ownership
  Catalogue --> Reviewer : akv_secret_entry records, each naming its mode and its consumers
  Terraform -> VaultWE : create each Terraform-managed secret with its computed expiry
  Terraform -> VaultNE : create the same secret in the regional pair
end

group F-004-US2 — SaaS credentials are replaced on a schedule without anyone handling them
  Rotator -> Rotator : validate TokenType, SecretName, both stores and the minter
  Rotator -> Status : IsActive
  Status --> Rotator : leadershipStatus active
  Rotator -> Saas : mint a new credential
  Saas --> Rotator : the new token value
  Rotator -> Writer : Put(secretName, value, RecoverIfSoftDeleted)
  Writer -> VaultWE : set secret
  VaultWE --> Writer : secret_write recorded
  Writer --> Rotator : nil
  Rotator -> Writer : Put(secretName, value, RecoverIfSoftDeleted)
  Writer -> VaultNE : set secret
  VaultNE --> Writer : secret_write recorded
  Writer --> Rotator : nil
end

group F-004-US3 — a rotation does not break a consumer mid-flight
  Rotator -> Rotator : SleepWithContext for the grace period, 24 h by default, interruptible
  Rotator -> Writer : DisableOldVersions(secretName) on each regional store
  Writer -> VaultWE : disable every superseded akv_secret_version, deleting none
  Writer -> VaultNE : disable every superseded akv_secret_version, deleting none
  Rotator -> Metrics : saas_token_age_days for the rotated secret, read from the West Europe vault
end

group F-004-US4 — one write path, with predictable failures
  Rotator -> Writer : every write goes through the SecretStore interface; no caller builds its own request
  Writer -> VaultWE : set secret through the shared transport seam
  VaultWE --> Writer : success, or a status the seam maps to one of the four typed sentinels
  Writer --> Rotator : nil, or ErrSecretNotFound, ErrAuthFailed, ErrConflict or ErrSoftDeletedSecretExists, with the response body redacted
end

group F-004-US5 — no platform secret sits without an expiry
  Terraform -> Terraform : compute the expiry from the 90-day rotating quarterly boundary
  Terraform -> VaultWE : every platform-managed secret carries that expiration date
  ExpiryGate -> Catalogue : scan the Terraform secret resources for a null expiry
  Catalogue --> ExpiryGate : every entry carries an expiry
  ExpiryGate --> Reviewer : exit 0
end

== Failure modes ==

group failure — this cluster is not the active management cluster
  Rotator -> Status : IsActive
  Status --> Rotator : leadershipStatus standby
  Rotator --> Reviewer : ErrSkippedNotActive, logged and exited 0; nothing is minted and no vault is written
end

group failure — minting the new credential fails
  Rotator -> Saas : mint a new credential
  Saas --> Rotator : error
  Rotator --> Reviewer : the run aborts naming the token type; neither vault is written
end

group failure — the West Europe vault write fails
  Rotator -> Writer : Put(secretName, value, RecoverIfSoftDeleted)
  Writer -> VaultWE : set secret
  VaultWE --> Writer : error
  Writer --> Rotator : typed error; the run aborts before the second write, leaving the pair unchanged
end

group failure — the North Europe vault write fails after the first succeeded
  Rotator -> Writer : Put(secretName, value, RecoverIfSoftDeleted)
  Writer -> VaultNE : set secret
  VaultNE --> Writer : error
  Writer --> Rotator : the run aborts with the regional pair inconsistent
  Rotator -> Rotator : the scheduled job retries on failure, minting a fresh credential and rewriting both vaults
  Rotator --> Reviewer : eventually consistent, not atomic; the skew alert covers an exhausted retry budget
end

group failure — the process is cancelled during the grace period
  Rotator -> Rotator : SleepWithContext observes the cancelled context
  Rotator --> Reviewer : returns the context error within a second; superseded versions stay enabled
end

group failure — disabling superseded versions fails
  Writer -> VaultWE : disable superseded akv_secret_version records
  VaultWE --> Writer : error
  Rotator --> Reviewer : logged and not fatal; the run still reports success with the new version live
end

group failure — the destination secret is soft-deleted and the strategy is the default
  Writer -> VaultWE : set secret with the Overwrite strategy
  VaultWE --> Writer : conflict, then the probe finds a deleted-but-recoverable secret
  Writer --> Rotator : ErrSoftDeletedSecretExists; nothing is revived
end

group failure — the vault refuses the credential
  Writer -> VaultWE : set secret
  VaultWE --> Writer : 401 or 403
  Writer --> Rotator : ErrAuthFailed, with no secret value and no response body in the error
end

group failure — the vault returns a server error
  Writer -> VaultWE : set secret
  VaultWE --> Writer : 5xx
  Writer -> VaultWE : up to 3 retries, 200 ms backoff doubling to a 5 s cap, 5xx only
  Writer --> Rotator : a redacted error once the budget is spent
end

group failure — a platform-managed secret has no expiry
  ExpiryGate -> Catalogue : scan for a null expiry
  Catalogue --> ExpiryGate : an entry without an expiration date
  ExpiryGate --> Reviewer : NULL_EXPIRY_MODE=advisory reports and exits 0; NULL_EXPIRY_MODE=block exits non-zero. CI runs advisory today.
end

note over Rotator, Writer
  invariants: DOM-004-R1, DOM-004-R2, DOM-004-R3, DOM-004-R4, DOM-004-R5, DOM-004-R6,
  DOM-004-R7, DOM-004-R8, DOM-004-R9, DOM-004-R10, DOM-004-R11
  timeout 30000 ms per outbound attempt, in the shared transport seam
  retry: 3 attempts, 5xx only, backoff 200 ms doubling to a 5000 ms cap; no 4xx is retried
  grace period 86400000 ms by default, interruptible within 1000 ms of shutdown
  expiry: every platform-managed secret carries the 90-day quarterly boundary
  idempotency: the secret name plus the vault's own versioning — a repeated Put adds a version
  degraded: a standby cluster skips the run and exits 0; a failed disable is logged, not fatal;
  a write that fails between the two vaults leaves a skew bounded by the job's retry budget,
  alerting above 600000 ms — DOM-004-R3 is eventual consistency, not atomicity
end note

@enduml
